# Sender local parts, matched against the From header's local part by
# the local_sender_localpart rule in multimap.conf. Regular
# expressions, one per line.
#
# The campaign generates its addresses from a small vocabulary and a
# random number - kontakt62685@, info75620@, suite97212@, top2566246476@
# - which covers 118 of the 139 messages filed into TrainSpam in the
# month to 2026-09-04, and 1 of the 11932 messages in every folder this
# account keeps (the same INBOX message the domain map catches).
#
# The four-digit minimum is what makes this safe. `info@` and
# `support@` are the most ordinary addresses there are; `info64628@`
# is not one, and nothing in the archive uses a numbered variant of
# any of these words.
/^(?:kontakt|info|suite|top|support|service|market)\d{4,}$/i
